nd resilience risks.\n- Work closely with Technology and Operations to ensure DORA and operational resilience requirements are embedded by design.\n- Maintain oversight of Business Continuity and Disaster Recovery frameworks.\n\nCommercial & Strategic Risk\n- Support new products, partnerships and market expansion through proactive risk assessment.\n- Provide commercially pragmatic advice that enables innovation while protecting the organisation.\n- Review strategic initiatives from an enterprise risk perspective.\n\nRisk Monitoring & Reporting\n- Develop Key Risk Indicators (KRIs), risk dashboards and management reporting.\n- Maintain the corporate Risk Register and oversee remediation of risk actions.\n- Coordinate stress testing, scenario analysis and periodic risk assessments.\n\nLeadership & Culture\n- Build and lead a high-performing Risk function.\n- Promote a strong risk culture through education, engagement and collaboration.\n- Work closely with Compliance, Financial Crime, Internal Audit and all first-line business functions.\n\nIdeal Background\nThe ideal candidate will have significant experience leading Risk Management within a regulated payment institution, electronic money institution, or banking environment. Experience establishing risk frameworks within a growing organisation, together with the ability to balance robust governance with commercial ambition, will be highly valued. We are seeking a builder who enjoys creating capability from first principles rather than simply maintaining an established framework.\n\nEssential Experience\n- Senior risk management experience within a regulated financial services environment.\n- Strong understanding of Enterprise Risk Management, Operational Risk, IT Risk and Risk Appetite frameworks.\n- Knowledge of DORA, EBA Guidelines, PSD2/PSD3 and broader European regulatory expectations.\n- Experience presenting to Boards, regulators and senior executive management.\n- Excellent stakeholder management and leadership capability.\n\nHighly Desirable\n- Experience supporting a regulatory licence application or launch of a regulated financial institution.\n- Knowledge of merchant acquiring, payments, Open Banking and embedded finance.\n- Experience implementing Governance, Risk & Compliance (GRC) technology platforms.\n- Professional risk qualifications (IRM, PRM, FRM or equivalent).\n\nPersonal Attributes\nStrategic, intellectually curious and commercially pragmatic. An independent thinker with excellent judgement and the confidence to provide constructive challenge where required. A collaborative leader capable of influencing across all levels of the organisation whilst maintaining the highest standards of integrity, professionalism and accountability.\n\nMeasures of Success (First 12 Months)\n- Establish Paytm Europe's Risk Management Framework prior to commercial launch. \n- Develop and implement the Company's Risk Appetite Statement and Risk Register. \n- Embed effective risk governance and reporting across all business functions. \n- Support successful regulatory authorisation and readiness for CSSF supervision.\n- Establish a strong risk culture that enables sustainable commercial growth. \n- Build a scalable Risk function capable of supporting Paytm Europe's European expansion.\n\nWhy This Role Matters\nEffective risk management will be fundamental to Paytm Europe's ability to innovate, grow and maintain the confidence of regulators, customers, partners and shareholders. The Head of Risk will play a central role in ensuring that robust governance becomes a competitive advantage, enabling Paytm Europe to expand confidently whilst maintaining the highest standards of resilience, accountability and operational excellence.",
